WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.880 --> 00:00:06.100
The first trailer for Black Widow, the solo
vehicle for the heroic Avenger, is finally

00:00:06.100 --> 00:00:08.970
here, and it is pretty spectacular.

00:00:08.970 --> 00:00:12.701
There's plenty to unpack in the spot, but
with all of the insane action, there are a

00:00:12.701 --> 00:00:15.070
few details that you may have missed.

00:00:15.070 --> 00:00:17.909
Fortunately, we're pretty good at spotting
those.

00:00:17.909 --> 00:00:22.679
The trailer opens on a panoramic view of a
city, one which might not be immediately familiar

00:00:22.679 --> 00:00:24.230
to American eyes.

00:00:24.230 --> 00:00:28.599
That statue in the center of the shot is pretty
distinctive, however, and if you already have

00:00:28.599 --> 00:00:33.420
a gut feeling as to what this setting might
be, let us go ahead and confirm it for you.

00:00:33.420 --> 00:00:37.990
That installation is called the Liberty Statue,
and it watches over the great Hungarian capital

00:00:37.990 --> 00:00:38.990
of Budapest.

00:00:38.990 --> 00:00:41.970
Now, a few of you may be asking, "So what?"

00:00:41.970 --> 00:00:46.010
For the rest of you, we'll give you a second
to pick your jaws up off the floor.

00:00:46.010 --> 00:00:50.720
You'll recall that, during the absolute mayhem
that was the Battle of New York in 2012's

00:00:50.720 --> 00:00:55.600
The Avengers, Natasha Romanoff and Clint Barton
had a humorous exchange while they were smack

00:00:55.600 --> 00:01:00.150
dab in the middle of shooting and arrow-ing
the heck out of the invading Chitauri hordes.

00:01:00.150 --> 00:01:03.360
"This is like Budapest all over again!"

00:01:03.360 --> 00:01:06.350
"You and I remember Budapest very differently."

00:01:06.350 --> 00:01:10.079
It seems highly unlikely that this would be
a mere coincidence.

00:01:10.079 --> 00:01:14.000
It's also worth noting that after this shot
dissolves to a montage of previous Marvel

00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:18.420
films, with Romanoff's voiceover wistfully
recapping the road to her "family" in the

00:01:18.420 --> 00:01:22.479
Avengers, the first recognizable character
we see is Barton.

00:01:22.479 --> 00:01:25.149
Will Hawkeye join in on the action in Black
Widow?

00:01:25.149 --> 00:01:27.990
We feel pretty safe in guessing that he will.

00:01:27.990 --> 00:01:32.689
After a very Widow-y Marvel Studios card,
we see Romanoff arriving at Budapest's train

00:01:32.689 --> 00:01:36.899
station, followed by a shot of what appears
to be a convoy of military vehicles headed

00:01:36.899 --> 00:01:38.549
to an unknown location.

00:01:38.549 --> 00:01:43.710
We then briefly see who is leading that convoy:
General Thaddeus "Thunderbolt" Ross, who is

00:01:43.710 --> 00:01:46.240
not the biggest fan of the Avengers.

00:01:46.240 --> 00:01:51.090
You'll recall that during Civil War, Romanoff
was on the pro-registration team led by Iron

00:01:51.090 --> 00:01:52.090
Man.

00:01:52.090 --> 00:01:56.170
However, during the enormous brawl at a German
airport, she had a slight change of heart,

00:01:56.170 --> 00:02:00.659
allowing Captain America and Bucky Barnes
to escape, while the rest of Cap's anti-registration

00:02:00.659 --> 00:02:04.310
team was captured and hauled off to the Raft
super prison.

00:02:04.310 --> 00:02:08.170
Romanoff's role in helping them skedaddle
would not have been lost on Ross, who almost

00:02:08.170 --> 00:02:12.550
certainly has designs on making sure she ends
up cooling her heels in the Raft, as well.

00:02:12.550 --> 00:02:17.070
Of course, we know that she eventually joins
Rogers and Sam Wilson on the run, ending up

00:02:17.070 --> 00:02:21.200
in Scotland, where we catch up with the trio
during the first act of Avengers: Infinity

00:02:21.200 --> 00:02:22.200
War.

00:02:22.200 --> 00:02:25.860
This likely means that Ross won't have any
luck bringing the Black Widow in, but that

00:02:25.860 --> 00:02:28.930
doesn't mean he won't be a major thorn in
her side.

00:02:28.930 --> 00:02:34.210
The spot finally gives us our first look at
an iconic Marvel villain: Taskmaster, who

00:02:34.210 --> 00:02:39.330
in the comics is capable of perfectly replicating
the fighting style of anyone he might encounter.

00:02:39.330 --> 00:02:43.520
The baddie's super-muscle memory also allows
him to use any weapon after observing its

00:02:43.520 --> 00:02:47.950
use just once, and you will notice that in
the Black Widow trailer, he's using a weapon

00:02:47.950 --> 00:02:52.950
that we've only ever seen one MCU character
employ before, a character who just happens

00:02:52.950 --> 00:02:55.550
to have very close ties to Romanoff.

00:02:55.550 --> 00:02:59.910
We suppose this could be a coincidence or
a mere aesthetic choice, but we do find it

00:02:59.910 --> 00:03:04.400
a bit odd that Taskmaster would be channeling
Barton in his first appearance in the trailer.

00:03:04.400 --> 00:03:08.430
We'd also like to point out that we're using
the descriptor "he" because Taskmaster is

00:03:08.430 --> 00:03:12.630
male in the comics, but it's not at all clear
that this is the case here.

00:03:12.630 --> 00:03:16.380
The actor portraying the villain hasn't been
disclosed, and it stands to reason that this

00:03:16.380 --> 00:03:20.320
is a detail that Marvel has been keeping under
lock and key for a reason.

00:03:20.320 --> 00:03:25.280
The Taskmaster of the MCU could very well
be female...and could, in fact, even be one

00:03:25.280 --> 00:03:27.110
of Romanoff's "family."

00:03:27.110 --> 00:03:31.710
As we see in a brief scene around a dining
room table, this family includes Yelena Belova,

00:03:31.710 --> 00:03:35.680
with whom Romanoff has a nice, friendly fight
near the opening of the spot and with whom,

00:03:35.680 --> 00:03:40.750
at points in the comics, Nat shares the Black
Widow moniker; Alexei Shostakov, AKA the Red

00:03:40.750 --> 00:03:46.160
Guardian, Russia's answer to Captain America;
and Melina Vostokoff, whom we first see briefly

00:03:46.160 --> 00:03:48.310
wearing a very Widow-y outfit.

00:03:48.310 --> 00:03:52.410
We know that Belova and Vostokoff are products
of the same "Red Room" training that molded

00:03:52.410 --> 00:03:57.310
Romanoff into a deadly weapon, but in Vostokoff's
case in particular, we don't necessarily know

00:03:57.310 --> 00:03:58.970
what her motives will be.

00:03:58.970 --> 00:04:03.270
In the comics, Vostokoff is known as the Iron
Maiden, and she is driven by a deep-seated

00:04:03.270 --> 00:04:07.460
hatred of Black Widow, whose shadow she has
never been able to escape.

00:04:07.460 --> 00:04:11.569
She's even tried to assassinate Romanoff,
so if the character indeed remains an ally

00:04:11.569 --> 00:04:16.509
throughout this film, it will represent a
complete 180 from her comics incarnation.

00:04:16.509 --> 00:04:20.190
We were heartened to see that David Harbour,
who has earned household name status thanks

00:04:20.190 --> 00:04:25.410
to his role as Chief Jim Hopper in Stranger
Things, didn't get crazy jacked for his role;

00:04:25.410 --> 00:04:30.280
indeed, he's just as doughy, yet he still
manages to squeeze into his old suit to join

00:04:30.280 --> 00:04:32.560
the ass-kicking party.

00:04:32.560 --> 00:04:33.560
"Yeah!

00:04:33.560 --> 00:04:34.840
Ahahahahaha…Still fits."

00:04:34.840 --> 00:04:41.150
And kick ass, he does, in a very brief shot,
we see him going toe to toe with Taskmaster,

00:04:41.150 --> 00:04:45.810
an extremely dangerous opponent if ever there
was one, and holding his own.

00:04:45.810 --> 00:04:50.130
Unfortunately, we only see a literal second
of the fight, but if we're being honest, all

00:04:50.130 --> 00:04:54.100
we can hope for is that it isn't the last
scene in which Red Guardian appears.

00:04:54.100 --> 00:04:58.630
Harbour is an extremely endearing actor, his
few appearances in this trailer have us anxious

00:04:58.630 --> 00:05:03.040
to see more of Shostakov, and that old costume
even looks pretty badass.

00:05:03.040 --> 00:05:06.700
But it's obvious that the Guardian hasn't
seen action for quite some time.

00:05:06.700 --> 00:05:10.230
There have to be some high stakes involved
in Black Widow, and what we're saying here

00:05:10.230 --> 00:05:25.030
is that we really, really hope that the Guardian
survives this fight, unlike…well…

